## Self-calibration (in-cleaning loop) — make it work well & properly
  Code: Cleaner.image_gen / Cleaner.self_cal_cycle (image_generation/image_maker.py)
        main_calibrations.self_cal_cycle (data_calibration/main_calibrations.py)

 - Solution strategy
   - Solint schedule: start long (scan / 'inf') and shorten each cycle (inf -> 60s -> 30s -> 'int')
     as SNR/dynamic range improves. Today Cleaner.self_cal_cycle never passes solint, so
     main_calibrations.self_cal_cycle always uses 'inf'. Wire options.solint -> per-cycle solint.
   - Phase-then-amp progression: run several phase-only (calmode='p') cycles first, then a final
     amp+phase (calmode='ap', solnorm=True to preserve the flux scale) ONLY once the model is good.
     Doing 'ap' too early corrupts fluxes. (self_cal_cycle is phase-only right now.)
   - Faint-source SNR: set minsnr on the self-cal gaincal (none set today); allow gaintype='T' and/or
     combine='spw' to boost SNR when per-spw 'G' solutions fail.

 - Convergence & safety (currently absent)
   - Actually stop: image_gen computes improvement_score but the `break` is commented out, so it runs
     every cycle even while diverging. Implement a real stop criterion.
   - Keep-best / rollback: self-cal can make things worse — track the lowest-RMS cycle and revert
     rather than always using the last cycle's image.
   - Gating: only self-cal when the target is bright enough (use MIN_FLUX_FOR_SELF_CAL and the image
     peak/RMS dynamic range, not just the NED check); skip/abort cleanly on faint targets.
   - Flagged-fraction monitor: applymode='calflag' flags solution-less data; report % flagged per
     cycle and bail if excessive.

 - Reference antenna
   - Replace "3rd closest by vibes" (find_refant -> anntennas_list[3]) with a principled pick:
     central, low-flagging, present the whole track. Choose once and FIX it across all cycles.

 - Solution bookkeeping / model
   - Decide & document the scheme: each cycle re-solves from raw DATA vs the latest MODEL and applies
     only the newest caltable (non-incremental). Either keep that consistently or go incremental
     (gaincal gaintable=[prev...], applycal all accumulated tables). Confirm which column tclean
     images each cycle (initial_cycle images DATA; self-cal cycles image CORRECTED after applycal).
   - Inspect/record solutions: implement check_refant (currently pass); optionally plot gain phase/amp
     vs time and save per-cycle stats for archiving.

 - Code cleanup
   - Consolidate duplicates/stubs: self_cal_solint_variation duplicates self_cal_cycle;
     find_solint_variations (image_maker) and phase_self_calibration (main_calibrations) are empty.
   - Wire find_solint_variations into the solint schedule above.

 - Manual self-cal mode
   - Implement the 'manual_self_cal' breakpoint: pause to let the user inspect image/gain solutions
     and choose solint/calmode/continue-or-stop before each cycle (delineate from interactive clean).
